PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round-0 responses converge on same core arithmetic: absorbed power = I*(W/e)≈6.79e-11 W (W/e=33.97 J/C), m_air=3.515e-4 g=3.515e-7 kg from focused beam (0.018 cm²×15.1 cm) and ρ=1.293 mg cm⁻³, yielding Ḋ_air≈1.93e-4 Gy s⁻¹; multiply by supplied 0.02 s scan factor → ~3.87 μGy surface dose to tissue (μ_en/ρ equivalence assumed). 

Errors noted: several colleagues report nGy (missed g→kg conversion); two report mGy (mass off by 10³–10⁶); Colleague 16’s explicit μ_en scaling to full beam power is superfluous and incorrect (current already measures absorbed energy directly). Monochromator aperture, 33 keV, and tabulated μ_en/ρ never needed once current and focus geometry are known. 

Consensus value is therefore 3.87 μGy; unit-conversion mistakes explain the spread. No prior private belief to update.}

